lines=['# #028E Review packet — Complete locally','','Base: accepted `bd3169d857373a06cbbe90241b187752a0c26c95`, branch `feature/local-environment-setup`. Local commit only; no push or deploy. **0 Higgsfield credits and 0 real provider calls.** No new npm dependencies. #028F is not started.','','## Live reviews: Joe’s decision','','Published Google/Yelp feeds remain live. The approval version covers contractor-controlled layout, variants, copy, media, settings and review display/source settings, including `minReviewRating` and show/hide. Provider review text, new reviews, counts and averages are excluded; live changes never invalidate approval.','','The packet saves dated evidence labeled **“Reviews shown at time of review — live reviews may differ.”** It never replaces the published feed. Same-version replay reuses the original snapshot. Filtering still applies only to displayed reviews; averages/counts use all real reviews, and zero after filtering omits the section. A mocked feed update proves the published count changes from 4 to 5 and the average from 3.5 to 4.4 while approval and the old evidence remain unchanged. No real provider was contacted.','','## What changed','','- Shared section films use the existing lazy ambient player: silent looping inline playback, poster until playing, offscreen pause, reduced-motion/static fallback and a styled pause/play button. Native browser controls were removed. The installed movie and the shared #028B2 section content are unchanged. The embedded editor preview loads the same treatment.','- Generated mid-sentence service vocabulary is sentence-cased, preserving acronyms and proper/custom names. All 17 trades and four Looks are covered.','- At phone widths the floating chat/project actions stay out of the hero, so its headline, focal image and primary action remain uncovered. They return below the hero; the project dock also clears the final contact section. Static/no-JS actions stay in normal flow.','- Generated/saved versions prepare private review folders containing source/manifest hashes, public HTML, both-width screenshots, five frames for each installed clip, legal/financing/consent text with page and selector, design/copy/media picks, rights references and Sample/provided classification. Publicly excluded sample/draft projects, closed forms, disabled pricing and unavailable retained authored pages are omitted using the public eligibility rules. The enabled guide landing page is included.','- The new staff screen at `/admin/review-packets/:siteId` uses the existing light `bv-` components and local fonts. It shows screenshots, clip frames, claims, provenance, checklist and exact-version approve/reject decisions. Rejection requires a reason; approval requires all checklist acknowledgements. A contractor cannot approve their own packet.','- Website, project, page, form, blog and visibility publication require approval for the exact proposed content. Controlled edits and regeneration invalidate it. An atomic content comparison also prevents stale publication if a related record changes during the backup. Existing authorization, CSRF and validation checks remain.','','## Capture and approval contract','','The version hash covers the full saved contractor-controlled source; the #023 manifest digest is recorded separately as `manifestHash`. Each folder is tied to both. Approval records include approver identity, UTC timestamp, version/manifest hashes, decision and reason. Evidence file hashes are verified before approval and publication.','','Local capture is a host binding, implemented in `src/aws/review-capture.js`. Configure `REVIEW_BROWSER_MODULE` with an already installed Playwright module and optionally `REVIEW_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE`, or pass a capture binding to `createRuntime`. It installs nothing and contacts no remote generation service. An unconfigured host honestly shows **Local browser capture is not connected** and blocks publication. Runtime/deployment configuration was not changed outside the repo. See [infra guidance](../../modules/infra.md).','','Page screenshots use a stable reduced-motion state; clip motion is documented separately at 0%, 25%, 50%, 75% and the last decodable frame near 100%. The packet contains the complete Playbook checklist. Visual judgments remain **Needs staff review** until staff explicitly acknowledges them; this is not the future #028F automated QA certification. Saved HTML, captures and snapshot reproduce byte-for-byte in the forced replay test, apart from capture timestamps.','','## Five Sample proof packets','','These are clearly fictional local fixtures, not real contractors or publicly deployed sites. Their proof approvals identify the test reviewer and are not Joe’s production approvals.','','| Sample fixture | Version / packet | Pages | Screenshots | Clip frames | Claims |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
