lines+=['','### Protected output and permitted differences','','All existing CSS, including `platform.css`, remains byte-identical. Of 280 protected raw outputs, 212 are byte-identical; 68 homepages contain only the authorized Part 1 player/polish markup. Of 374 archived responses, 306 are byte-identical and 68 have the same approved Part 1 change. The exact normalizer reverses only that known markup and asset inclusion; every normalized hash matches. Raw and normalized hashes are retained in `after-sites.json` and the checks. No general whitespace/content normalization was introduced.','','The original renderer bodies, section variants, scroll logic and Roofing CTA sources remain unchanged. The only review-feed source change prevents an audit database write during isolated packet rendering; normal published feed reads and behavior remain unchanged.','','### Contrast, diagnostics and test prerequisites','','The inherited narrow platform console allowlist is unchanged. Non-allowlisted platform diagnostics: **0**; new staff-screen warnings/errors: **0**. Expected protected-frame/explicit failure-fixture entries remain separately logged. Public negative-fixture diagnostics recorded by the optional legacy platform collector are reported separately in the quality summary, not silently added to an exception. The dedicated public matrices have zero page exceptions. No real external provider or font-provider calls were made.','','The legacy suites now need an approved-version prerequisite for successful publication. `tests/helpers/review-approval-fixture.mjs` is explicitly preloaded only by the legacy runners: after the real gate denies a missing packet/approval, it supplies a clearly marked capture double and exact-version test approval, then retries. Existing permission, validation, state and behavior assertions are retained. It is never loaded by the 46 real packet checks, the live-review/approval contract tests, or the staff browser suite. Its synthetic PNG is not screenshot evidence.','','Legacy test changes:','','- `cinematic-films.mjs` and `engagement.mjs`: replace the old native-control/eager-autoplay expectation with silent inline looping, lazy source and the custom control. Asset and content checks remain.','- `hero-editor.mjs`, `planning-ambient.mjs`, `planning-scroll.mjs`, `promotions-ambient.mjs`, `promotions-scroll.mjs`, and `roofing-polish-part2.mjs`: apply the shared exact Part 1 normalizer before their existing protected-HTML assertions.','- `website-pages.mjs`: accept the new version-bound `review_approval` record, requiring a valid approval and SHA; original opt-in and record-behavior checks remain.','','The final full-suite pass includes a strict Roofing acceptance recheck: the first attempt observed a 4px early-load desktop overflow, which did not recur with the original assertion unchanged (913 checks, 132 page states, 0 failures). No CSS or timing tolerance was changed to obtain the pass. Both logs are retained; the initial measurement is not hidden.', '', 'A cleanup-only failure in the first media run was fixed in the evidence redirector: deleting its temporary marker now targets the mapped #028E file, never #028D. Six boundary checks prove the original path remains untouched. The original failed attempt is retained separately; both commands were rerun and passed in the final table.', '', 'Existing tests that write old evidence are redirected to this ticket. The four historical pending-film tests run with their original pending catalog fixture; the installed catalog is restored byte-for-byte in `finally`, followed by a build. The old FFmpeg path is temporarily redirected to the already installed executable and its test file restored. No old evidence or downloaded executable is committed.','','## Every command','','Commands ran from `C:\\Users\\joe\\website_creator`. Named `npm run build` and `npm run typecheck:client` were also run successfully.','','| # | Command | Result | Log |','|---:|---|---|---|']
